Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 12:29:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 133/143] arm64: dts: allwinner: t527-orangepi-4a: enable the
 IR receiver

The Orange Pi 4A has an IR receiver window on the board, wired to the
SoC CIR input on PL11, served by the CIR instance in the RTC power
domain.

Enable that instance and mux its RX signal to PL11, following the
X96Q Pro+ pattern from the upstream A523 CIR series.

The wiring is confirmed by the vendor's Android 13 device tree for
this exact board (s_irrx@7040000 status "okay" with PL11/"s_cir",
irrx@2005000 disabled).  The vendor Linux BSP board file instead
enables irrx@2005000 on PH19, but PH19's mux 2 is the CIR *output*
per the BSP pinctrl table (cir_in lives on PI8 mux 3), so that
combination cannot receive anything and looks like template rot.

Co-Authored-By: AI Agent
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
index b91edba00..c8146f45c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
@@ -487,6 +487,12 @@ &pio {
 	vcc-pk-supply = <&reg_cldo1>;
 };
 
+&r_ir {
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&r_ir_rx_pin>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &r_i2c0 {
 	status = "okay";
 
